         8.6  tests/test_usage.py::test_the_footer_reads_the_recorded_provider_not_the_model_name
         recommended test: For a given configured model name, cache-breakpoint inclusion, batch eligibility, and credit attribution all agree with the single resolved provider. Overriding or changing that one decision changes all three consistently, and no provider-dependent code path parses the model name itself.
           inputs:  A ModelClient with a batcher (MessageBatcher or fake transport) and the default completion fn. Use monkeypatch to override the single provider decision: patch llm.provider_of to return a made-up provider (e.g. 'acme') for a model like 'acme/model-x', and separately patch llm._needs_explicit_marker to return True/False for the same model. Build the request through the client's completion path.
           detects: Batch eligibility re-evaluates `provider_of(request["model"]) == ANTHROPIC` inline instead of using the same decision (`_needs_explicit_marker`) that governs cache breakpoints. The two provider-dependent gates are separate comparisons on the model name. If the breakpoint decision changes (for example, an override or an added provider), batching will not follow it, so breakpoints and batch eligibility can disagree.
           full detail: acceptance recommendation --criterion provider-decision-single-source

