    [missing_case] provider-routing-by-model-name/unprefixed-name-no-provider
      A configured model name with no `/` (for example a bare `claude-...` name) yields provider None. Such a call is then treated as non-Anthropic: it gets no explicit cache marker, is never batched, and is not counted in the Anthropic spend, even though the name may identify Anthropic's models.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#0
      src/acceptance/llm.py#1
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 245 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] provider-routing-by-model-name/provider-prefix-case-sensitive-exact
      `provider_of` takes the raw text before the first `/` and compares it for exact equality with `anthropic`. A prefix that differs in case or has surrounding whitespace (`Anthropic/...`) is treated as a different provider, so provider-specific handling is skipped.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#0
      src/acceptance/llm.py#1
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 245 skipped once the defect was covered
    [other] provider-routing-by-model-name/recorded-provider-from-record-model
      The provider attached to an observed call is derived from the `model` taken from the record or transcript, not from the configured model name. A replayed call, or one whose record model differs from the configured name, can therefore carry a provider that does not match the configured model. A non-string model also silently yields None.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 2 skipped once the defect was covered
    [not_wired] provider-routing-by-model-name/batch-routing-divergent-check
      The batching decision calls `provider_of(...) == ANTHROPIC` directly instead of going through the shared helper `_needs_explicit_marker`. Provider-dependent dispatch is therefore decided at two separate sites, and they could diverge.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#1
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      pairs: 12 put to the model, 237 skipped once the defect was covered

  provider-decision-single-source
    [unenforced_on_one_path] provider-decision-single-source/batch-gate-bypasses-marker-decision
      Batch eligibility re-evaluates `provider_of(request["model"]) == ANTHROPIC` inline instead of using the same decision (`_needs_explicit_marker`) that governs cache breakpoints. The two provider-dependent gates are separate comparisons on the model name. If the breakpoint decision changes (for example, an override or an added provider), batching will not follow it, so breakpoints and batch eligibility can disagree.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#1
      src/acceptance/llm.py#3
      pairs: 249 put to the model, 0 skipped once the defect was covered
    [scope_too_narrow] provider-decision-single-source/provider-field-missing-on-some-call-records
      Credit attribution reads `call.get("provider")`, which is set only in one place that builds an observed-call record. Calls built elsewhere (embeddings, Jev, other clients, or records whose model is not a str) get provider None. Those calls are silently left out of the Anthropic credit figures, even though the model name states Anthropic.
      src/acceptance/llm.py#2
      src/acceptance/usage.py#4
      pairs: 4 put to the model, 245 skipped once the defect was covered

  spend-excluded-from-review-state-and-report
    none enumerated: The diff keeps spend out of review state and the report. `report_usage` calls `print(..., file=sys.stderr)`, so the footer goes to stderr and is never returned or stored. In `measure_instability`, it is called before `InstabilityReport` is built, and its result (None) is not passed in. The new `provider` key is added only to the in-memory observed-call dicts, and `clients` holds only client objects. The new `anthropic_*` fields live on `StageUsage` and `RunUsage`, which are usage models, not review state or report models. `render` is the footer renderer, not the report renderer. Nothing in the diff writes spend into `Review`, `RunSnapshot`, `InstabilityReport` or the provenance, so no static path violates the invariant.

